  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Wetskills Challenge 2024</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Wetskills competitions will bring diverse young talents from South Africa, Southern Africa and beyond with a passion for Water &amp; Sustainability together to co-create new solutions for water challenges in among others KwaZulu Natal Province, specifically Durban, in a two-week period.In an interactive and intergenerational workshop, the teams will present their innovative and out-of-the-box solutions for water challenges to a jury panel and audience. The winning team will be awarded at the WISA conference in Durban on 12-14 June 2024.The aim of this project is to involve local and Dutch private sector companies working on the Circular Economy and Green Hydrogen and water nexus in the Wetskills Challenge, by providing a case for young professionals to work on and provide some services such as training and being part of the jury, to build capacity of young people to make them more employable and to support network building with the private sector that could lead to potential employment opportunities.</narrative>
  </description>
